{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789256658,"nonce":"x/EL2lCA34h1Oa7icolykuf5B6I=","title":"zrtl_plugin! trips unexpected_cfgs in a crate without the linked-into-host feature","message":"The macro in sdk/zrtl/src/plugin.rs gates its `_zrtl_info` and\n`_zrtl_symbols` exports on `#[cfg(feature = \"linked-into-host\")]`,\nevaluated in the invoking crate. A crate that invokes the macro without\ndeclaring that feature (zyntax_embed's static_plugin_registration test)\ngets `unexpected cfg condition value`, which `-D warnings` turns into a\nclippy failure for every embed `--tests` run.\n\nFix in the macro rather than in each invoker: emit the cfg through\n`::core::cfg!`-free means the lint accepts (`#[cfg_attr]` with an\n`allow(unexpected_cfgs)` on the item, or a `cfg` the macro's own crate\nowns and re-exports), so a plugin crate need not declare a feature it\nnever sets.","files":null}]}